Package: rankflex
Title: Flexible Framework for Multi-Source Ranking Aggregation and Visualization
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: c(
    person("Yang", "Li", , "124020251@link.cuhk.edu.cn", role = c("aut", "cre")), 
    person("Shiyu", "Xiong", , "123090673@link.cuhk.edu.cn", role = "aut"), 
    person("Ruowei", "Fang", , "122090862@link.cuhk.edu.cn", role = "aut")
    )
Description: Provides a general-purpose framework for integrating, aggregating, and 
    visualizing rankings from multiple sources. Users can import ranking data from 
    any domain (e.g., university rankings, movie ratings, or sports standings), clean 
    and standardize multi-source data, and apply custom weights to available indicators 
    to construct personalized composite scores. The package supports sensitivity 
    analysis of weighting schemes, weight optimization via linear programming to 
    maximize a target entity's composite ranking, comparison of custom rankings against 
    original sources to identify over- and under-rated items, and visualization through 
    both static snapshots and animated multi-year bar chart dynamics. A sample dataset 
    of global university rankings (QS, Times Higher Education, and ARWU, 2023–2025) 
    is included as a demonstration use case.
